<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0"><head><title>NPC and faction tracker</title></head><body>
<outline text="# NPC and faction tracker">
  <outline text="A living cast for a solo campaign. The base below is an interactive table (a /base) that opens on its Board view, grouped into faction lanes: click a cell to edit, and use the switcher at its top left for Table, Cards or Calendar. See npc-faction.md for the walkthrough."/>
  <outline text="## The cast">
    <outline text="Two things make the Board group by faction. The Faction column is marked as a Status column, and the factions themselves are declared as a state set by the pill below. Capitals are only a reading convention: a value becomes a lane because it is a declared state, so an undeclared faction lands in a &quot;No state&quot; lane instead. Drag a card (or Alt+Left/Right on a focused card) to move an NPC between factions as loyalties shift."/>
    <outline text="{seq Cast: UNDERCITY FREEPORT ASHCHURCH | GONE}"/>
    <outline text="The states left of the bar are the factions in play; anything right of it reads as finished, which is what GONE is for: an NPC who is dead, fled or written out. A sequence needs at least one state on each side of the bar."/>
    <outline _type="base" _colrole="[null,&quot;status&quot;,null,null]" _view="{&quot;kind&quot;:&quot;board&quot;,&quot;groupBy&quot;:1}" text="| NPC | Faction | Disposition | Tie |&#10;|---|---|---|---|&#10;| Vex the Fence | UNDERCITY | wary | owes you a favor |&#10;| Mara Coil | FREEPORT | ally | your old crewmate |&#10;| Prior Aldous | ASHCHURCH | hostile | wants the relic |&#10;| Sig One-Eye | UNDERCITY | neutral | sells information |"/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Scene beats that link to the cast">
    <outline text="In your own game, give each NPC their own point in the outline (outside the base) and link scene beats to it by typing `[[` and picking the point. The NPC's point then shows a backlink to every scene that mentions them, so you can navigate both ways. The two beats below carry real links: open Vex the Fence and its Linked from panel lists the scene."/>
    <outline text="Vex the Fence" _id="npc00010">
      <outline text="You slipped [[#npc00010|Vex]] a coded note under the bridge. She read it, burned it, and named a price: {2d6} silver. Tag the thread #relic so you can pull every beat that touches it later."/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Prior Aldous #relic" _id="npc00020">
      <outline text="[[#npc00020|The Prior]]'s people were watching the docks. An oracle to see if he moved first: {Yes, and 1 | Yes 6 | Yes, but 3 | No, but 3 | No 6 | No, and 1}. Note what it says and move the scene."/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## How to run it">
    <outline text="Add an NPC: click into the base and type a new row, or press Alt+Shift+Down on a cell to insert one. Set their Faction to one of the declared lanes and the card appears there. For a faction that does not exist yet, add it to the `{seq Cast: ...}` pill first, or the card lands in &quot;No state&quot;."/>
    <outline text="Track a relationship shift: change the Disposition cell, or move the card to a new faction lane on the Board. The table is the truth, so both views always agree."/>
    <outline text="Find everyone in a faction: read the lane. The roster lives in base rows rather than points, so a search cannot pick a row out of it, and the Board lane IS the answer to &quot;who is in the Undercity&quot;. Search is for the NPC points and beats outside the base: tag them with #relic (or any thread) and click the tag to pull every scene that touches it."/>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body></opml>
